    "notationLabel": "Express Stave, 6-6 Jazz Font — reproduction study",
    "notationFootnote": "",
    "author": "John Keller",
    "description": "Reproduction study — inspired by Express Stave, 6-6 Jazz Font (John Keller, 2009). Same tritone D/G# staff and inverse-7-5 solid/hollow fill as the Pianoforte version, with an added subtle 6-6 pattern via notehead SHAPE — one whole-tone set slanted, the other a flat (horizontal) oval (per the operator reference; the flat set uses a distinct flat-oval glyph, not a conventional notehead). The slant glyph is the default oval sheared 0.5 (geometric approximation). Keller's custom D clef (E1) is exercised in register-label (text) mode showing 'D'; the published clef glyph is deferred as an asset. Same continuous-grid D-ledger deviation as the Pianoforte fixture; half/whole side strokes not in this single-duration preview. Built from the public gallery description/image; not endorsed by or derived from the original.",
    "systemName": "Express Stave, 6-6 Jazz Font",
    "systemCreator": "John Keller",
